WEBVTT

00:16:29.662 --> 00:16:32.954
and we can teach the model, behave more
like this and less like that.

00:16:33.454 --> 00:16:35.871
And it works better than I
ever imagined it would.

00:16:36.246 --> 00:16:40.662
And that gives me a lot of hope that
we can build an aligned system.

00:16:40.912 --> 00:16:41.996
We'll do other things, too,

00:16:41.996 --> 00:16:47.704
like I think curating data sets where
there's just less sort of bad data to

00:16:47.704 --> 00:16:49.287
train on. It will go a very long way.

00:16:49.662 --> 00:16:51.329
And as these models get smarter,

00:16:51.329 --> 00:16:53.537
I think they inherently develop

00:16:53.996 --> 00:16:56.496
the ability to sort out bad
data from good data.

00:16:56.496 --> 00:16:57.621
And as they get really smart,

00:16:57.996 --> 00:17:00.621
they'll even start to do something
we call active learning,